da one interesting thing is  that the text mentions actual gameplay  situations which i found to be quite  intriguing and hints at the type of  stuff we might be seeing in the game it  states that quote therefore for example  the passing through movement allows the  player character to quickly escape from  an underground cave or quickly move on  to the roof from the inside of a  building moreover when there's a cave  beneath a building where the player  character cannot enter because the  entrance door is locked the passing  through movement allows the player  character to enter the building from the  cave i don't know about you but the  scenarios described here really get me  excited i especially like the idea of a  house or building that's locked from the  inside and gaining access to it by  phasing through the ceiling of an open  space or cave located underneath it it's  definitely gonna make you think about  the environment in a completely  different way and has a lot of potential  for hidden secrets we may have even  already seen a hint of this in the 2021  teaser remember that underground cave  where link is seen fighting that weird  ceiling monster thing i mentioned in an  earlier video that the aesthetics of  this area are very similar to the one  seen on top of the floating islands with  the same grey pillars and such and  although we don't have all the  information about the room given the  camera angle so far there's no clear  sign of a doorway leading in and out of  it meaning he could have accessed it  through the floor and the only way out  is through the ceiling so perhaps some  of the islands won't just have stuff on  top of it but on the inside as well the  mechanic itself will consist of four  separate stages the neutral position  when link hasn't activated the ability  the ready position which is when the  ability is activated but not triggered  yet the active position when link is  moving up and through the ceiling object  and the destination position when he  emerges on top of the object and goes  back into neutral position in many ways  it's very similar to the way the sheikah  slate works minus the destination  position  [Music]  according to the description the passing  through movement can only be performed  if a series of conditions are satisfied  these include a movement condition  height condition ceiling condition  destination condition and object  condition the movement condition is  simply the demand that the player is in  possession of whatever allows the  mechanic to be executed this is also  referred to as the movement item which  is basically the same thing as a  progression item although it's called an  item it's safe to say that it likely  refers to the powers that link receives  from his new green glowing arm rather  than a physical item like in the older  games again very similar to the sheikah  slate runes in breath of the wild when  will be able to obtain this power  remains to be seen but without it link  won't be able to perform the move next  is the height condition which kinda  speaks for itself it dictates the  maximum amount of vertical distance link  will be allowed to traverse using the  ability prior to performing the move i.e  during the ready position the game will  detect if there's anything above the  character in video game engines this is  commonly achieved by using a method  known as raycasting as the name suggests  when raycasting the engine will project  one or more invisible lines or rays from  a predetermined origin point and with a  certain length direction and angle when  the ray hits one or more objects in the  game world it'll store various types of  data which can be recalled later things  like the name of the object the distance  between the object and the origin point  and even the angle at which the ray  intersects with the surface and this is  where this illustration comes into play  according to the description six rays  will be casted up from a hexagonal shape  surrounding the base of the character  and the length of these will represent  the height condition if the rays don't  intersect with anything it means that  there's nothing within range located  above link and the jump cannot be  executed and if they do the height  condition will be satisfied it doesn't  mention what the maximum height will be  but it does state that in some specific  scenarios the height condition may be  different or even ignored if there's no  place to be excluded such as a place far  above in the game a height limit need  not be set alternatively the height  limit in the height condition may be set  to an infinite or sufficient height  which means that there is substantially  no height limit so i guess there's  moments in which link will be allowed to  travel up a lot higher or as the text  says without limits this could be  referring to a situation where link uses  the ability to travel between the  surface and the sky for instance  obviously these islands are very very  far above hyrule and in a situation like  this one temporarily disabling the  height limit makes sense in a way you  could compare it to skyward swords  parasail in most scenarios link can only  descend slowly with it or get a small  boost from a gust of wind for as high as  it allows but when traveling to the sky  he is able to cover a massive vertical  distance albeit in a cutscene in this  case maybe there will be pedestals or  something like it located on the surface  from which link can travel to a  designated island but i do suspect that  it's only reserved for very specific  moments under normal circumstances like  in a dungeon setting or during regular  exploration the height limit will likely  always be active we might be able to  upgrade the ability like we did with the  sheikah runes making it possible to  travel higher in later parts of the game  but we'll just have to wait and see the  ceiling condition will judge if the  bottom surface of an object is suitable  for link to pass through this is  determined by the shape as well as  link's position relative to it for  instance if link is too close to the  edge parts of his body would be sticking  out so the condition is not satisfied  same goes when a part of the ceiling  protrudes perpendicular to it and link  overlaps with it in the case of  irregularities in the shape of the  ceiling the condition will be determined  based on the angle if an incline is too  steep link won't be able to pass through  either this is also why six rays are  being casted instead of just one as they  will be needed to calculate the surface  angle in three dimensions then we have  the destination condition which is  pretty much the same thing as the  ceiling condition except for the top  part of the object instead the only  unique aspects to this condition is that  it takes into account whether or not  link will be able to fit in the space  he's traveling to and if there's more  than one passable object located above  link two for instance the destination  may be set to the second object instead  of the first so if object one meets the  ceiling condition but doesn't meet the  destination condition and object 2 meets  both it's possible to pass through  object 1 into object 2 and then emerge  at the destination there which is quite  interesting  [Music]  lastly we have the object condition this  one is more or less an additional  restriction that can override all  previous conditions it simply means that  even if the height position angle and so  on are all satisfactory an object may  still be restricted from passing through  in the illustration this is demonstrated  by a spiked surface but i'd imagine  there will be many more ways to do it  like malice or some other hazard or  perhaps the ability doesn't work for  objects made from a certain material a  bit like the walls inside the sheikah  shrines and the divine beasts which were  unclimbable for no reason other than the  challenge would be negated if they were  climbable and don't tell me they're too  slippery or something ever tried  climbing solid ice with your bare hands  not easy yet link here doesn't even  break a sweat figuratively speaking  obviously this last condition is simply  here so the level designers can prevent  us from completely breaking the game's  progression though i'm sure speedrunners  will find a way as they always do and  finally let's go over some of the  visuals real quick in the video about  the time reversal mechanic i mostly  skipped over visual related stuff  because well we already saw what it  looks like in a teaser for this mechanic  however we only see the tail end of it  we get a very brief glimpse of link  soaring upwards in sort of a diving  position him hitting the ceiling and  crawling inside it and then emerging  from the floor on top of the island the  text elaborates on some of the other  visual elements as well as the camera  positions and optical tricks used before  and during the execution of the move  during the ready position a pillar of  light extending upwards will surround  the character model this is not the same  thing as the raycasting we talked about  earlier by the way as those are  invisible unless you're in debug and  only relevant for the engine to perform  its calculations the only loose  connection it has to it is that the  light pillar will allegedly have the  same vertical length so it's basically a  visual indicator to communicate to the  player where the height limit is this  also brings us to this illustration at  first i had no idea what i was even  looking at here and even the description  of it doesn't really make it clear it's  a follow-up from figure 16 which shows  the character in a neutral position  standing between a floor and a ceiling  the ceiling is indicated by a grid which  is also what we see in figure 17 except  here it's seemingly facing the camera  and has some sort of circle projected on  it so here's the deal the description  states that when the character goes into  the ready position the camera will snap  into an upwards facing position behind  the character a bit like how the camera  snaps to an over the shoulder view when  link draws his bow this way the player  can visually scan the ceiling to find a  suitable spot to pass through the circle  is simply an indicator that shows if the  part of the ceiling you're currently  under is passable or not probably by its  color in the illustration the camera is  pointing straight up at the ceiling and  link himself is not visible but the text  also explains that this might differ  slightly for the final product stating  that quote in the example shown in  figure 17 the player character is not  displayed in another embodiment a part  for example head of the character may be  displayed when a virtual camera is  directed upward the virtual camera may  not necessarily be directed straight  upward and may be oriented such that the  ceiling located above the character is  included in the field of view it doesn't  say if we'll be able to adjust the  camera manually after it's snapped into  position but we'll just have to wait and  see it's likely prone to change during  the development stage depending on what  they find to be the most user-friendly  method to perform the action lastly we  have a little visual trick something  they'll use while link is moving through  an object in the teaser we simply see  the camera panning upwards following  link's movement as he enters and then  emerges from the island while this is  happening link temporarily disappears  from the camera view and we continue to  see the outer walls this matches with  example b shown in figure 18 where the  camera is located outside the object  however as we can see with example a  there will be situations where the  object link is moving through is large  enough that the camera has no space to  back away causing it to move inside the  object with him obviously this kind of  situation is inevitable not only in the  case of a large object but if he's in a  room or cave as the text exemplifies the  camera would have no other choice but to  move through the floor in breath of the  wild when you move the camera inside of  an object in most cases it'll become  partially or completely invisible this  is because of a thing called backface  culling or bfc which is when only one  side of a polygon is rendered so if  you're looking at it from the other  direction where the camera isn't  supposed to be you see nothing this  reduces the amount of polygons the  engine needs to draw and makes rendering  objects quicker and more efficient in  the old days you could move the camera  inside of a house for instance and you  would still see an interior but in  modern games you do not either way it  goes without saying that if the camera  moves inside of an object while link is  moving through it it's gonna look weird  even if they would render the inside  it's just gonna look like a hollow space  the solution presented is that in these  situations the game will place a  background image behind the character  one that will always face towards the  camera and covers its entire field of  view obstructing the real visuals going  on in the background this background  image will likely be a representation of  the material of whatever object link is  moving through like a rock floor for  instance the only example from another  zelda game i can think of from the top  of my head is a link between worlds when  link goes inside of a wall to travel  between dimensions this too is obviously  just an animated background image and  that's about it for the mechanic as  always thank you so much for watching a  shout out to my awesome discord  community and to my amazing patreons and  channel members you guys are the best  that is all for now i hope to see you in  the next video this is dawn signing off  and have a good one  [Music]  you

